  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "## 12.4.0\n\n### Features\n- Bookmarks round-trip, so links into the document navigate after loading and after saving. `{\\*\\bkmkstart name}` names the paragraph holding it (`Block.Bookmarks`) and is written around every named paragraph; a link to a bookmark reads from and writes as `HYPERLINK \\l \"name\"` (`HYPERLINK \"file\" \\l \"name\"` reads as `file#name`). It was written as `HYPERLINK \"#name\"`, which Word treats as a file name. A markdown heading that a link targets by its slug is written as a bookmark under that slug.\n\n### Fixes\n- A markdown heading or code block (or any block kind registered for a `Paragraph` subclass) is written as a paragraph. The writer recognised only the built-in paragraph kind and dropped these blocks with their text.",
